R-SO14 R-SO15 R-FE4 R-LF1 R-DL1 R-DL3 R-DL4 R-DL5 R-DL10 R-NI5 R-NS2 R-NS3 R-EF1 R-EC13 R-EC15 R-EC10 R-CC4 R-CC3 R-HF1 (slice 072b): `Fetch.packages!` with `Choose` and nothing installed, no `roc` on PATH (`have: path:none`): R-SO14 picks the compiler, asks (R-NI5), downloads it and sets `default-roc`. The list has 3 nightlies (14, 16 and 18 of October, all old enough). `compat.tsv` has facts for 2 package hashes: HA passes on 16 and fails on 18, HB passes on 14, 16 and 18. Each run fetches another package (so its download happens).
Run 1 (the base URL of the GitHub API gives a transport error, and no list is cached yet): exit 15 (R-DL5: no list can be read). The package was downloaded before (the program is chosen after the downloads, R-FE4), and its temp dir is deleted.
Run 2 (R-SO14 case 1, `none:project:HA,HB`, TALON_AUTO_INSTALL=yes): no `ask`, no `tty`. The list is read, one `db_query` with `facts=6` (2 hashes, 3 compilers), the newest compiler that passes for HA and HB is the 16th (not the latest, the 18th). The 16th is installed (lock, download, extract, chmod, compat check, `.talon.json`, rename), and `default-roc` is written (config.toml is made: the lock, 2 reads, `write_atomic`). `roc unbundle` runs with the 16th: `fetched`.
Run 3 (case 1 with a hash that has no fact, `none:project:HC`, the mode needs the terminal, which is one: `tty`, the answer is `y`): the latest (the 18th). One `ask` with the prompt text of R-NI5 (it names the compiler and that it becomes the default). The default is set already (run 2): the lock, one read, unlock (it is kept, the text of config.toml does not change).
Run 4 (`TALON_AUTO_INSTALL=no`, no flag): exit 13 before the list is read again: no request, no `db_query`, and no compiler call. Run 5 (R-SO14 case 2, outside a project: the default scope of the entry; the answer is `n`): the list (from the cache of run 2, R-DI2), the prompt, exit 13 (declined). Nothing is installed, no default change.
Run 6 (`CI=true`, no consent): the mode is non-interactive, so no prompt: exit 13 with the size of the download (R-DL1, the text of `Consent.download_stop`). Run 7 (`TALON_NIGHTLY=false`): the domain has no release, exit 10, the text names the switch (R-NS2).
Not in this case: `--offline`. An offline fetch never downloads a package, so it never reaches the choice of the program. The row is in the L0 test of `NoRank.gate`.
